WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.180
You build a wall, we tear it down!

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:03.920
Send them home!

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:05.820
Send them home!

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:09.039
No issue is more hotly contested today then
immigration

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.540
with restrictionists calling for the deportation
of all illegals

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.560
and a 50% cut in legal immigration.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:18.740
Here are the 5 strongest arguments against
immigration

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:19.880
and why they're wrong.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.720
So with immigration, you better be smart and
you better be tough,

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:26.360
and they're taking your jobs and you better
be careful.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.020
So which is it President Trump?

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:32.400
Do we have record low unemployment or are
immigrants stealing all the jobs.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.120
The worst case estimates are that low skill
immigrants

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.180
reduce the wages of high school drop outs
by less than 5%.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:42.840
That's not nothing, but immigrants make things
cheaper for all Americans

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.740
by doing jobs such as picking fruit or cleaning
up on construction sites.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.820
The money saved can be devoted to other productive
uses,

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:51.760
which also creates jobs.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.660
In the developed world there is no correlation
between unemployment and immigration rights

00:00:56.660 --> 00:01:00.840
Immigrants go to hot economies and they leave
when the jobs dry up.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:02.200
Why would you want to bring a people

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.420
who are immediately dependent on welfare when
they get here?

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.880
Don't you want people who add something immediately
to your country?

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.220
Since the late 90s, most legal immigrants

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.960
and all illegals are barred from receiving
most forms of welfare.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:18.459
The only real taxpayer funded services most
immigrants use

00:01:18.459 --> 00:01:22.799
are emergency medical treatments that account
for less than 2% of all health care spending

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.020
and K-12 education for their children who
are often US citizens.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:30.960
Immigrants that do qualify for programs such
as medicaid food stamps

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:33.000
or supplemental social security,

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:38.020
use these programs at lower rates than native
born Americans or naturalized citizens.

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:43.020
Legal immigrant men also have a higher labor
force participation rate than natives.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:47.260
And illegals are even more likely to be working
than legal immigrants.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:49.179
They're here illegally, they're not paying
taxes, okay?

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:50.840
I've heard this one before too, I hear them all.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:54.180
Legal immigrants pay the exact same taxes
as all Americans.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:58.500
Illegals pay the exact same sales and property
taxes and between half and two thirds

00:01:58.509 --> 00:02:01.169
also end up paying payroll and income taxes

00:02:01.169 --> 00:02:05.500
because they use fake social security cards
and other documents to get hired.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.460
And if we want unauthorized immigrants to
contribute more in taxes,

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:12.800
the best way to accomplish that is to change
their legal status.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:16.220
What I would suggest they do is that they
go back to their home country,

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:19.440
get in line with the hundreds of thousands
of people from their home country

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.060
who are trying to do it legally.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:25.400
For many immigrants, especially for Mexico,
there really is no line.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:30.180
In 2010, for instance, just 65 thousand visas
were given to Mexicans

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:35.100
with the overwhelming majority going to close
family members such as spouses and minor children.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:38.420
The wait list had 1.4 million people on it,

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:41.960
effectively meaning there is no change of
ever getting in.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:46.740
Long wait lists also exist for the Philippines,
China, India and other countries

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:50.160
and for all the fear of what restrictionists
call 'chain migration'

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.540
family reunification consists almost exclusively

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:58.300
of US citizens bringing their spouses and
unmarried minor children to live here.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:03.480
The backlogs for most countries means that
this can take between 15 and 25 years.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:07.940
If you start to bring your sister over when
she's 25, you'll be lucky to welcome her

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:09.660
by the time she turns 40.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:14.000
You should not import people numerous enough
to influence your society,

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.140
change it's laws and destroy your culture.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:17.820
Exactly the same complaints were made

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:21.000
about newcomers like the Irish, the Jews and
the Italians.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:25.240
Yet about one third of Mexican immigrants
marry outside their ethnicity or race,

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:28.660
which is the same percentage as it was a quarter
century ago.

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:32.400
Successive generations also see massive gains
in household income

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.700
and home ownership rates.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:39.460
And when it comes to learning English,

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:44.800
all signs are that Hispanics are more likely
to speak English at home than years past.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:49.720
By the third generation English is the dominant
language in three quarters of Hispanic homes.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:53.880
Which is the same rate of language shift seen
in earlier waves of immigration.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:56.120
The bottom line is that when it comes to immigration

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:58.980
the instincts of the American people are correct.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:03.100
Immigrants help the economy and newcomers
make the land of opportunity

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.420
a better place to live.

